AFAIK it actually stands for Mobile OBject (or alternatively MObile 
oBject, or alternatively MOBile object ;), as MUD code tracks players, 
monsters, NPCs etc. as "objects". Mobs are just a subclass of objects 
that happen to be mobile.

Note - this is not to assert that MUDs are object-oriented; most are not.

